15. Safety and AI Response Handling
Generative AI systems can produce incorrect information, so EduGenie should explicitly account for this limitation. Google also notes that Gemini can make mistakes. Google Help 
FR-23: AI Response Warning
The interface should communicate that AI-generated educational content should be verified, particularly for important academic information.
________________________________________
FR-24: Inappropriate Content Handling
The system should detect and appropriately handle requests that are outside the educational purpose or violate application safety rules.
________________________________________
FR-25: Error Handling
If Gemini cannot generate a response, EduGenie shall display an understandable error message rather than exposing technical details.
Example:
"EduGenie couldn't generate a response right now. Please try again."
________________________________________
16. Search/Grounding Requirement
If EduGenie includes web-grounded answers, the system may use Gemini API capabilities such as Google Search grounding to obtain current information. Google's Gemini API documentation describes Google Search as a built-in tool for grounding responses in current information and reducing hallucinations. Google AI for Developers 
FR-26: Information Grounding
For appropriate queries, the system should retrieve supporting information and present relevant sources.
This should be treated as an optional advanced feature, not necessarily a core MVP requirement.
