20. Security Requirements
Security is particularly important because EduGenie may store user accounts, conversations, uploaded documents, and educational information.
NFR-SEC01: Authentication
Only authenticated users should access protected account information.
NFR-SEC02: Authorization
Users should only access resources permitted by their role.
NFR-SEC03: Password Protection
Passwords should never be stored as plain text.
NFR-SEC04: Secure Communication
Communication between client and server should use HTTPS/TLS.
NFR-SEC05: API Key Protection
Gemini/API credentials must not be exposed in frontend code.
The AI API should be accessed through a secure backend service.
NFR-SEC06: Input Validation
User input should be validated before being processed.
NFR-SEC07: Data Protection
Personal and educational data should be protected against unauthorized access.
For institution-based deployments, the applicable Google Workspace/Gemini education privacy and administrative controls should also be considered. Google's current education documentation describes enterprise-grade data protection for Gemini for Education in supported Workspace contexts. Google for Education+1 
